# R5 FINDINGS: issues in every auto run (board 366516b)

Scope: 7 run folders under `master_chat_tasks/auto/runs/` (1 old night.py run + 6 auto.py runs), `auto.py` (1521 lines), `AUTO_POLICY.md` (59 lines), `PLAN_TEMPLATE.md` (14 lines), `tools/issue.py`, `board.json`, `registry/tasks.json`, `decisions.jsonl` (409 lines), `master_queue.py`, `run-with-subscription.sh`, the 17:41 cold-chain run log, and `~/.local/share/opencode/log/opencode.log` (read-only python scan; written `oc.log:N` below). No code was edited. Experiments ran on a copy of auto.py in `/tmp/R5-auto-1/` with fake `AUTO_*` paths; the script is kept as [exp1.py](file:///Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal%20Bench/master_chat_work/20261028_upgrade/R5_auto_issues/exp1.py).

Main finding: **the shared Claude subscription limit hit 5 of the 7 runs, and auto.py saw it as a stall in none of them.** Opencode retries a rate-limit error inside the session, so the session stays "busy". auto.py counts every non-idle status as busy (auto.py:299-301), and it only classifies an error once a message finishes with it (auto.py:447-457). The overnight run lost about 32 worker-hours to two silent stalls. Its REPORT noticed only the second one and gave the cause as unknown.

Labels: VERIFIED = seen in a file or tool output. INFERRED = reasoned from evidence. UNVERIFIED = not checked.

