79:## 3. Usage limits and a budget per day
103:## 4. Policy gaps (AUTO_POLICY.md / PLAN_TEMPLATE.md)
105:- AUTO_POLICY:37 (PAUSED on limit/network) assumes auto.py sees the limit. It never did (R5-01). Add: "A LIMIT event means: hold spawns and harness adds; do not send continue; wait for LIMIT CLEARED."
106:- AUTO_POLICY:46 "hard caps 4 workers" vs auto.py:65 5 (R5-19). Proposed: "Caps come from auto.py limits (now 5 workers, 2 harness); PLAN.md may set lower; budget rule in section Budget."
108:- AUTO_POLICY:15 (harness only via auto.py) conflicts with plan wind-down runs (R5-10). Proposed: "During wind-down, a paid run is allowed only for a task named in PLAN.md `Wind-down:` and via `auto.py harness --wind-down`."
109:- AUTO_POLICY:30 (override round limits) does not cover the issue.py time box (R5-08). Proposed: "issue.py time-box refusals: override with `--by "master (auto)" --override "AUTO plan step: <line>"`; REPORT gives the count, not each line."
110:- AUTO_POLICY:32 (one corrective message) has no case for doom_loop or ContentFilter (R5-06). Proposed: "doom_loop: one continue telling the worker to add a rising counter to polls; ContentFilterError: one continue with 'shorter output'; a second error of the same kind → skip, Needs Ayush."
111:- AUTO_POLICY:54 says decisions need `"by"`, but the file uses `"who"` (R5-19, R5-23).
112:- No rule for "worker server not answering" (R5-07): "Check `auto.py status` once; if the server is up, record a transient; if down 2 polls, `auto.py resume` is Ayush's call."
113:- No last-spawn cutoff (R5-22), no budget (section 3), no stop-now procedure (R5-11).
114:- PLAN_TEMPLATE.md (14 lines: Until, Ayush words, Do in order, Do not, Timed steps) lacks fields: `Paid runs: N (day cap)`, `Workers / harness / Docker: a / b / c`, `Budget: workers while a run is RUNNING`, `Wind-down: <tasks allowed one step, until HH:MM>`, `Last spawn: HH:MM`. Timed steps at the start minute need R5-17.
116:## 5. Fix order
118:1. **Together, first (stops the biggest loss):** R5-01 retry detection + hold, R5-02 harness budget gate + early kill, R5-03 reset parsing and keying, R5-13 auth vs limit split. They touch auto.py poll/spawn/harness and master_queue tick/pause. Test with the fake opencode server and the test_master_queue.py stubs.
119:2. R5-04 + R5-05 (master retry note, stall watchdog). These reuse the R5-01 status read.
120:3. R5-07, R5-09, R5-11 (health debounce, FINAL conditions, stop --now) in one watcher change; R5-25 comes with stop --now.
121:4. R5-08 issue.py `--by` + time box rework, with the R5-23 decisions writer.
122:5. R5-10 + R5-22 + PLAN_TEMPLATE fields (wind-down / last spawn), plus the policy text from section 4.
123:6. LOW cleanups: R5-12, R5-14, R5-15, R5-16, R5-17, R5-20, R5-21, R5-24.
124:Risky: R5-02(d) kills a running paid run on a log line. Match only the exact `accounts exhausted` text and keep the job folder. R5-11 aborts sessions, so it must stay opt-in (`--now`). Changing the issue.py caps (R5-08) loosens a rule Ayush approved (24 Oct U1); it needs his yes (Q3).
126:## 6. Questions for Ayush
137:## Lessons for the master

