The lane logs show a meaningful tradeoff: warrant’s parallel gate finished sooner, but each long oracle run took longer than in the earlier serial gate. I also found that the cited cold-chain QC recheck used a sequential chain. I’ll quantify both from the saved timestamps and flag the limits of the comparison.
